(Yet Another Geek Pun)

I recently learnt that what I always called "anneau integre" in french
was, in english, called "cancellation ring" (*).

Then I spend a few time daydreaming about what we could do with that in
nethack...

(*) For those who don't want to look in Wiki, a cancellation ring is a
ring where the product of two non-0 numbers can never be 0 (ie 0 has no
divisors).

[For those who wonder how 0 could have divisors, a typical example of a
non-cancellation ring would be the ring of square matrices (any
dimension), with usual sum and product.]

